But too high experience is bad for you. The monsters will be generated
stronger.

> And magic marker, I guess if you can't cast spells you can't write
> them.

No. You can't write anything you haven't ID'd before (unless you're a
wizard). Also knowing the spellbook doesn't help you in writing the
scroll and vice versa.
 
> And also, what is the best place to identify item properties?

I don't understand your question. Scrolls/spells of ID work the same
everywhere and the BUC status can be checked by dropping the stuff onto
an altar. Gems can be ID'd by a touchstone or pseudo-ID'd by
engraving/throwing at unicorns. Wands can mostly be ID'd by engraving
and potions by quaffing (after you've ruled out polymorph and have a
unicorn horn handy). BTW. Never read unidentified scrolls unless you
know what you're doing.

